        <selectionEntry name="I Legion: Dark Angels" id="f504-3651-b642-7020" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="First Among Equals" id="4489-0c83-42ed-0642" hidden="false">
              <description>You may take one Dark Angels Heavy Cruiser, Battlecruiser, Assault Cruiser, or Grand Cruiser for every two Dark Angels cruisers, light cruisers, strike cruisers, or escort squadrons (of any type) in your fl eet, however, you cannot count more escort squadrons than capital ships for this purpose. (e.g. A Dark Angels fl eet with two cruisers and two or more escort squadrons can take two Heavy Cruisers, Battlecruisers, Assault Cruisers, or Grand Cruisers.)</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Legion of Secrets" id="c6ba-4ff7-f0a6-6573" hidden="false">
              <description>Enemy vessels reduce the “Enemy Contacts” command check modifi er for vessels with this special rule being on special orders by -1 Ld. (i.e. Vessels with Improved Sensor Array only receive a +1 Ld bonus.)</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Dark Age Weaponry" id="3cf0-000d-369e-31e9" hidden="false">
              <description>This rule only applies to any Dark Angels Legion Capital Ships that have been upgraded with the Turbo Weapons refi t.
When a vessel with this special rule fi res its lances and/or weapons batteries, for each To-Hit roll with a result of “6”, you may roll to hit again with the same weapon, however, these additional rolls to hit cannot themselves generate additional rolls to hit.
Vessels lose the benefi t of this special rule if they are crippled or if they are on All Ahead Full, Burn Retros, or Come To New Heading special orders.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Turbo Weapons (+5% ship cost)" id="43e8-644e-7c66-8ee4" hidden="true" import="true" type="upgrade"/>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="III Legion: Emperor’s Children" id="c79a-7800-902e-fa2b" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="2" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Exemplars of War" id="8e5f-959b-77a6-6b26" hidden="false">
              <description>As long as no ships or squadrons in your fl eet have failed a command check this turn (after any re-rolls), vessels with this special rule may re-roll To-Hit rolls with a result of &quot;1&quot;. Simply pick up the missed dice and roll them again - the second result stands, even if it is worse.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Marus Skara" id="a575-5aa4-4495-b264" hidden="false">
              <description>Once per battle at the beginning of your turn you may declare that you are executing the Marus Skara. For the remainder of this turn you may add +10cm to the speed of any vessel with this special rule.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Flawless Execution" id="c535-b3aa-98a5-ceac" hidden="false">
              <description>When a ship or squadron of ships composed entirely of vessels with this special rule performs a command check to go on a special order other than Brace For Impact! or to use its Maneuvering Thrusters, compare the result with the table below and apply the appropriate eff ects. Note: These eff ects are cumulative. (i.e. An Emperor’s Children vessel which rolls 3 or more below its modified leadership for a command check receives all the eff ects on the table.)


COMMAND CHECK RESULT
EFFECT
Equals or is below the ship or squadron&apos;s modified leadership
The ship/squadron is placed on the chosen special order as normal.
1 or more below the ship or squadron&apos;s modified leadership
The ship/squadron may perform teleport attacks even if the special order would ordinarily prevent this.
2 or more below the ship or squadron&apos;s modifi d leadership
If the special order reduces the eff ectiveness of the ship/squadron&apos;s weapons then its weapons are reduced by 25% (rounding up) rather than halved.
3 or more below the ship or squadron&apos;s modified leadership
The ship/squadron may perform an additional 45° turn at the end of its movement. All of the normal restrictions apply to this extra turn, meaning a capital ship must move its minimum turning distance again before making its additional turn (unless it is on Burn Retros special orders).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="IV Legion: Iron Warriors" id="285d-f209-539b-f80a" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="3" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Unbreakable Litany" id="3257-82ac-595a-4aa2" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule gain the following eff ects:
● Iron Within: At the beginning of this ship’s movement you may have it perform a leadership test. If it passes the ship does not suff er reductions to its speed for moving through blast markers (this includes gas, dust clouds, and similar eff ects). For vessels in a squadron make a single roll using the highest surviving leadership within the squadron.
● Iron Without: Successful To-Crit rolls against this ship must be re-rolled if the originating attack targeted its front arc.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Siege Batteries" id="e96e-ef3b-a2e7-9976" hidden="false">
              <description>This rule only applies to any Iron Warriors Legion Capital Ships that have been upgraded with the Superior Fire Control refi t.
Whenever a vessel with this special rule fi res its weapon batteries and bombardment cannons together, add both weapons’ fi repower together and look up the corresponding number of To-Hit rolls on the gunnery table. The diff erence between this combined number of To-Hit rolls and the Bombardment Cannons&apos; fi repower value are fi rst rolled by the Weapons Batteries, then the remaining To-Hit rolls are rolled by the Bombardment Cannons.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Fury of Olympia" id="fe22-7d9a-103d-eecb" hidden="false">
              <description>Ordnance markers launched by a vessel with this special rule re-roll To-Crit rolls with a result of &apos;1&apos;. Simply pick up the missed dice and roll them again - the second result stands, even if it is worse.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="V Legion: White Scars" id="8215-bb96-0b1c-a9ac" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="4" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier affects="entries.profiles.Unit" field="5.370656564232324e+29" scope="force" type="cumulative-add" value="5"/>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Masters of Maneuver" id="e45a-12f0-1e28-9860" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule receive a +1 Ld modifi er when attempting to go on All Ahead Full, Come to New Heading, and Burn Retros special orders</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Lightning Strike" id="462e-d521-2737-984a" hidden="false">
              <description>White Scars Legion Capital Ships with this special rule can perform teleporter attacks while on All Ahead Full, Come To New Heading, and Burn Retros special orders</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Swift as the Wind" id="f750-181e-718d-b608" hidden="false">
              <description>A vessel with this special rule adds +5  to its speed. Additionally, vessels with this special rule receive a +1 Ld modifi er when attempting to go on Brace For Impact!, Lock On, &amp; Reload Ordnance special orders.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="VI Legion: Space Wolves" id="9877-23f6-6b76-57be" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="5" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="No Prey Escapes the Wolf" id="e0c6-78ee-8eaf-13ef" hidden="false">
              <description>At the beginning of the enemy’s End Phase any ship or squadron with this special rule may attempt to go on No Prey Escapes special orders if there is an enemy ship both inside its front arc and within 15cm of its base. If it passes its command check the ship is placed on No Prey Escapes orders until the end of the turn, replacing any other special order it may be on currently.


Special Order: No Prey Escapes
A ship using No Prey Escapes orders must turn towards the enemy ship and move 4D6 cm forwards as if it were on All Ahead Full special orders. If any part of its base contacts any part of the target vessel’s base during the course of its movement it stops even if it has not moved its full distance. If the vessel going on No Prey Escapes special orders is a member of a squadron only one roll is made and every ship in the squadron moves the distance rolled. Once all ships on No Prey Escapes special orders have moved they must initiate a boarding action if possible.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Pack Hunters" id="8337-5600-ad37-cbc6" hidden="false">
              <description>When generating their starting leadership values, vessels with this special rule suff er a -1 Ld penalty. Furthermore, if you have already failed a command check this turn any vessels with this special rule which have yet to move may still attempt to go on a special order that any friendly ship with an embarked Space Wolves Praetor or Centurion is already on.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Beastial Savagery" id="8f74-45e4-f4ef-141c" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule and their ordnance markers may modify the result of their Hit-and-Run attacks by +1/-1 and receive +D3 to their rolls for determining the results of boarding actions.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="VII Legion: Imperial Fists" id="e2ac-e571-0341-667b" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="6" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Close Formation" id="504c-8ef2-61cc-4909" hidden="false">
              <description>A squadron comprised entirely of vessels with this special rule are considered in Close Formation when they are in contiguous base-to-base contact (i.e. you must be able to draw an unbroken chain of contact from any one ship’s base to any other in the group, the same way coherency is measured) and they are not on All Ahead Full or Come To New Heading special orders. While in Close Formation a vessels gain the following benefi ts:
● Wall of Flak: At the beginning of the Ordnance Phase before any ordnance markers have been moved a squadron in Close Formation may put up a Wall of Flak. If it does, it can use its turrets against both torpedoes and attack craft in the same Ordnance Phase, however, its turrets hit on the roll of a 5+ instead of a 4+. (Note: Remember that ships in base contact can mass their turrets as explained on page 80 of the Battlefl eet Gothic Remastered rulebook.)
● Hold the Line: When allocating hits against the nearest eligible ship in a squadron in Close Formation the Imperial Fists player may choose to allocate up to one hit to each of the other ships in the same squadron so long as they are in base contact with the nearest eligible ship.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Stalwart Obstinacy" id="b9ba-fa9f-6d94-0651" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule may still attempt to go on special orders if you have already failed a command check this turn, however, they suff er a cumulative -2 Ld penalty for each friendly ship or squadron that has failed a command check this turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Unshakeable Defense" id="0a88-cd12-eafb-1a37" hidden="false">
              <description>When a vessel with this special rule is on Brace For Impact! special orders it imposes a -1 to enemy Hit-and-Run attacks and it can perform Teleport Attacks. Furthermore, Brace For Impact! DOES protect against damage caused during a boarding action (including critical damage) for vessels with this special rule. (Note: The decision to brace for impact must be made before any dice are rolled to resolve the boarding action.)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="VIII Legion: Night Lords" id="895a-5f48-1934-4ebf" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="7" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Reign of Terror" id="d3d3-4185-fd89-9d03" hidden="false">
              <description>When a ship or squadron comprised of vessels with this special rule fails a command check you may choose for it to suff er a cumulative -1 Ld penalty for the remainder of the game to attempt the command check again rolling 3D6 and discarding the highest result, the result of the second roll is fi nal even if it is worse. Ships and squadrons can use this special rule so long as they have a leadership of 6 or more.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Cull The Weak" id="fb54-5c53-f6b1-360e" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule may re-roll To-Hit rolls with a result of &apos;1&apos; if the target vessel is crippled. Simply pick up the missed dice and roll them again - the second result stands, even if it is worse. Additionally, vessels with this special rule automatically pass any target priority checks to target vessels which are crippled or have a smaller maximum number of damage points.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Terror Tactics" id="fa4a-f56a-deeb-f96d" hidden="false">
              <description>When rolling to determine the result of a Hit-And-Run attack against capital ships or other targets that can suffer critical damage, you may choose to disregard the result of the dice and instead inflict a “Terror” critical hit. This rule applies to teleporter attacks from vessels with this special rule and ordnance markers launched by vessels with this special rule. Terror critical hits can be repaired with other critical hits in the end phase.


Extra Damage +0
Special Critical Hit
Terror: As they butcher the ship’s crew leaving grisly scenes of slaughter in their wake the Night Lords broadcast their screams over the intra-ship vox network to sow terror amongst the survivors.
The ship’s Leadership is reduced by 1 for each unresolved Terror critical hit it has suff ered.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="IX Legion: Blood Angels" id="6c6e-2e0d-d7f8-5208" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="8" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="On Angel’s Wings" id="4bb0-beca-d41b-b1d5" hidden="false">
              <description>On the turn they are launched Attack craft launched by vessels with this special rule gain +10 cm speed and are hit by turrets on a result of a 5+ instead of a 4+.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Encarmine Fury" id="0154-356d-6e73-7aa3" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule and their ordnance markers roll 2D3 when determining the result of hit-and-run attacks. If a double is rolled, choose which critical damage eff ect to apply out of the range of potential results for the Hit-and-Run attack after accounting for attacker and defender modifi ers.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="The Red Thirst" id="caa6-3a85-370b-e772" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule and their ordnance markers roll 2D3 when determining the result of boarding actions and hit-and-run attacks. If a double is rolled then regardless of the outcome of the boarding action the enemy vessel suff ers D3 damage.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="X Legion: Iron Hands" id="29c8-bcd9-5e13-4e18" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="9" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Adaptive Power Conduits" id="5f01-cdff-0e5f-371a" hidden="false">
              <description>When a vessel with this special rule fi res lances or weapons which use the gunnery table increase the number of dice rolled To-Hit by one, up to the total strength or fi repower values for the weapons being fi red listed on that ship&apos;s data sheet. This occurs after applying the reductions to the eff ectiveness of its weapons for any special orders or being crippled. For gunnery weapons the eff ect of Adaptive Power Conduits is applied before consulting the gunnery table to determine how many To-Hit dice are rolled for the attack.
Because power must be redirected from the ship’s engines to power its weapons, vessels with this special rule roll -1D6 cm when calculating their speed on All Ahead Full special orders.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Blessed Autosimulacra" id="569b-4b91-4959-dbc4" hidden="false">
              <description>The eff ects of any Armament Damaged critical hits suff ered by ships with this special rule are determined by the number of unrepaired Armament Damaged critical hits it has suff ered to the same location as follows:
● If the ship has suff ered a single port, starboard, prow, or dorsal armament damage critical hit the ship halves the eff ectiveness of that location’s armament until it has been repaired. The reduced strength or fi repower of any weapon eff ected by a single armament damaged critical hit is considered to be its new maximum strength or fi repower for the purposes of the Adaptive Power Conduits special rule until the armament damaged critical hit has been repaired.
● If the ship has two or more armament damaged critical hits to the same location then that location’s armament may not fi re.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="The Medusan Inheritance" id="c552-8739-648a-5312" hidden="false">
              <description>Ships in your fl eet that have been upgraded with an Archeotech Refi t may treat rare refi t options as normal refi t options and they may upgrade any Extremis Weapons they are armed with with the appropriate options from the table below for free. Additionally, when determining how many Extremis Weapons may be included in your fl eet you may take 1 more than the points value of your fl eet would usually allow.
Singularity Bombs: Once per game, when a vessel with this special rule fi res a Nova Cannon, after determining the fi nal location of the Nova Cannon template all vessels and ordnance markers within a 10cm radius measured from the template edge are caught in the singularity bomb’s gravity well. Ordnance markers within the gravity well are moved 2D6cm towards the center of the nova cannon template. Vessels within the gravity well must immediately perform a leadership test as if they were attempting to navigate through an asteroid fi eld, and any vessels that fail to pass the leadership test must move 2D6cm towards the center of the nova cannon template. After all vessels and ordnance markers within the gravity well have been moved or have passed their navigation test resolve the damage from the attack normally.
Graviton-Annihalators: When a vessel with this special rule fi res a Planet Scourer, in addition to its normal eff ects any vessel touched by the template cannot go on All Ahead Full, Come to New Heading, and Burn Retros special orders and reduces its speed by -5cm during its next turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XII Legion: World Eaters" id="7d26-72b3-f499-9f70" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="10" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Butcher&apos;s Nails" id="dde1-7d98-e362-4602" hidden="false">
              <description>If an enemy vessel is in the front fi re arc of a vessel with this special rule and within its maximum movement distance you must decide whether to give in to or resist the pull of the nails.
● Give In: the vessel with this special rule cannot declare special orders and must move into contact and initiate a boarding action if possible. When a World Eaters legion vessel initiates a boarding action because of this special rule the ship being boarded does not add its remaining turrets to its boarding value.
● Resist: A vessel with this special rule may attempt to resist the pull of the nails by taking a leadership test. If the test is passed then that vessel proceeds with its turn normally, however, it suff ers a -1 Ld penalty for command checks until the end of the turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Brute Simplicity" id="2711-6c9c-159b-21d4" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule (including escorts) may be upgraded with Ursus Claws for free and reduce the cost of Boarding Torpedoes by -5 points, however, your fl eet may never contain more than one Nova Cannon.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Violence Incarnate" id="2cc9-5873-a16f-fe61" hidden="false">
              <description>A vessel with this special rule doubles the result of its dice roll to determine the result of a boarding action.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XIII Legion: Ultramarines" id="1c53-dfe1-5fdb-606e" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="11" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Unity of Purpose" id="b34c-7f0c-d602-77ea" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule automatically pass target priority checks to target ships that have already been targeted this turn by a vessel in your fl eet with this special rule. Furthermore, when trying to declare a boarding action against an enemy ship that is already engaged in a boarding action with one of your ships, vessels with this special rule may increase their speed by 5 cm if doing so would allow them to move into base contact with the enemy ship.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Tactical Flexibility" id="cf26-5af9-02f5-099d" hidden="false">
              <description>Instead of being formed into squadrons at the beginning of the game as normal capital ships with this special rule may be formed into squadrons at the beginning of each of your turns as outlined in the forming squadrons section of this book. Capital ships formed into squadrons in this way remain in their squadrons until the beginning of your next turn. If the ship your Fleet Commander is embarked upon is destroyed then ships with this special rule may not be formed into squadrons on the following turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Certainty and Resolve" id="35e3-d985-3da5-2501" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule may attempt to go on Reload Ordnance special orders even if they would not normally be able to do so, rolling 3D6 and discarding the lowest result for their command check if they do. (ie: If they were on Brace For Impact! special orders or if you have already failed a command check this turn.)
72 of</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XV Legion: Thousand Sons" id="59b5-999e-4d1b-fe68" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="13" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Cult Arcana" id="40fd-1ad3-7b66-4981" hidden="false">
              <description>At the beginning of each of your turns each Thousand Sons Praetor and Centurion in your fl eet may attempt a cult ritual. Declare which cult ritual they are going to perform and then perform a leadership test using that commander’s ship’s leadership as if it were attempting a command check. If the test is passed apply the eff ect of that cult’s ritual to all vessels with this special rule in your fleet.
See page 80 of 221</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Sorcerous Translocation" id="a0a2-b151-1499-234a" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule increase the range of their Teleporter Attacks by +10cm.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Psychic Brotherhood" id="f550-bee8-1250-1cf2" hidden="false">
              <description>A vessel with this special rule ignores leadership penalties from any source except a Bridge Smashed critical hit as long as it is within 15cm of at least three other friendly ships with this special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XIV Legion: Death Guard" id="2777-c660-0c69-7387" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="12" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier affects="entries.profiles.Unit" field="4.869747323232344e+27" scope="force" type="cumulative-add" value="1"/>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Barbaran Endurance" id="c468-61d2-1c30-62db" hidden="false">
              <description>Capital ships with this special rule increase their maximum number of damage points by one. Because of their increased mass, vessels with this special rule roll one fewer D6 when calculating their speed on All Ahead Full special orders</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Sevenfold Numerology" id="d387-f0b3-0c91-20b7" hidden="false">
              <description>On your turn whenever an unmodifi ed result of “7” is rolled on any 2D6 roll you may remove one blast marker from the table, however, each blast marker you remove requires one more “7” to have been rolled than the previous removed blast marker. Blast Markers in contact with ships’ bases may not be removed, but otherwise you are free to choose which ones will go.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Unrelenting" id="fd56-a663-a8d4-f940" hidden="false">
              <description>A ship with this special rule which loses half its damage points is not crippled until it loses one additional damage point.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XVI Legion: Sons of Horus" id="6e9a-c8ea-9ea4-a1ef" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="14" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Armour of Pride" id="cc06-3f03-d883-1daf" hidden="false">
              <description>The fi rst time a vessel with this special rule that has embarked a Praetor or Centurion is reduced to 0 damage points the controlling player must immediately make a Leadership test for that model. If the test is failed then the vessel is destroyed as normal. If the test is passed then the vessel is not removed, but remains in play and regains D3 damage points.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Death Dealers" id="52ec-cf86-b5cf-98c7" hidden="false">
              <description>Ships with this special rule do not suff er a rightward shift on the gunnery table when fi ring through blast markers against targets within 30cm.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Merciless Fighters" id="125c-02d8-0db3-ca4f" hidden="false">
              <description>When a capital ship with this special rule performs a teleporter attack against an enemy vessel it receives a +1 modifi er to its Hit-and-Run attack for every friendly vessel with this special rule within 10cm of the target vessel (Max of +3).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XVII Legion: Word Bearers" id="ad76-0514-b1fe-e3ff" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="15" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Fanatical Zeal" id="54ae-e26b-275a-3000" hidden="false">
              <description>If a vessel with this special rule has fewer damage points than its starting number of damage points, it may re-roll a number of to-hit dice equal to half the number of missing damage points when attacking, rounded down to a minimum of 1. For each re-roll the vessel rolls in this manner, it rolls one fewer D6 when attempting to repair Critical Damage until its next turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Leaders of the Faithful" id="5576-1591-352c-ddfb" hidden="false">
              <description>When a ship or squadron comprised of vessels with this special rule fails a command check, if you use a commander’s re-roll from a Word Bearers Praetor or Centurion to attempt the command check again roll 3D6 and discard the highest result, the result of the second roll is fi nal even if it is worse.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="True Believers" id="5651-9d09-0093-e67b" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule cannot have their leadership reduced by more than -2 by any source except for a ‘Bridge Smashed’ critical damage. Furthermore if one or more vessels with this special rule are involved in a boarding action that results in a ‘Drawn Combat’ they are counted as having won the boarding action by 1 point.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XVIII Legion: Salamanders" id="c025-acff-a07e-b2f9" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="16" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Promethean Gift" id="5acd-1005-5196-38c5" hidden="false">
              <description>When a vessel with this special rule or one of its ordnance markers infl icts a critical hit you may discard the critical hit result and replace it with a ‘Fire!’ critical hit if either of the following scenarios has occurred:
● A critical hit is rolled which cannot be applied. (e.g. a prow weapon critical hit on a ship with no prow weapons.)
● A critical hit is rolled for a location which has already suff ered a critical hit (both repairable and non-repairable).</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Blood of Fire" id="42e0-27a9-70b3-0b2b" hidden="false">
              <description>When a Capital Ship with this special rule suff ers a critical hit before applying the critical damage result you may choose to perform a leadership test. If the test is passed the vessel suff ers a ‘Fire!’ critical damage result instead. Each vessel with this special rule may only use it once per turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Obsidian Forged" id="c820-a32d-3d73-3aad" hidden="false">
              <description>Each ‘Fire!’ critical damage that a vessel with this special rule fails to repair (extinguish) in the end phase only infl icts 1 point of damage to the ship on a D6 result of &quot;5+&quot; instead of automatically.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XIX Legion: Ravenguard" id="133e-d08d-1476-0067" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="17" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="For Whom the Bell Tolls" id="110b-debf-df56-a288" hidden="false">
              <description>Vessels with this special rule and their ordnance markers re-roll To-Hit rolls and Hit-And-Run attacks with a result of “1” against ships or squadrons which have embarked a Fleet Commander or Subordinate Commander. Simply pick up the failed dice and roll them again - the second result stands, even if it is worse.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="The Hidden Blade" id="cba2-1023-0cbf-67aa" hidden="false">
              <description>During the Set-Up step of the game you may declare that any number of Ravenguard legion vessels with a combined cost no more than a third of your fl eet’s points value is laying in wait for an ambush, holding any vessels designated as ambushers off the table as reinforcements. If the scenario being played already holds a portion of your fl eet off the table as reinforcements then when declaring which vessels will be ambushers you must choose vessels that are already being held off the table as reinforcements fi rst before choosing vessels from the rest of your fl eet.
At the beginning of each of your turns you can decide whether or not to spring the ambush. If you do, all ambushing vessels move onto the battlefi eld from any table edge or celestial phenomena, however, no vessel may enter the table within 15 cm of an enemy vessel (though once on the table they can move within 15cm of an enemy vessel). While moving ships entering play this way ignore the eff ects of celestial phenomena they pass through unless they end their move within it.
As they were operating at minimal power to evade detection the ambushing ships count as being in base contact with 1 additional blast marker until the beginning of your next turn. Do not actually place a blast marker, just make a note to reduce the ship’s shields by -1, its speed by -5 cm, its Ld by -1 for command checks, as well as the eff ects for damage control and boarding actions. Lastly, because their crews are too occupied reawakening the machine spirits, ambushing vessels cannot declare any special orders until the end of your turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Surgical Strikes" id="c1a7-af0d-9697-3fa2" hidden="false">
              <description>When a vessel with this special rule attacks an enemy ship that is moving away all of its gunnery weapons benefi t from an extra left column-shift in addition to any other column-shifts that apply.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="XX Legion: Alpha Legion" id="9877-39a7-a969-7532" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="18" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Lies and Obfuscation" id="b793-774d-d95b-98c0" hidden="false">
              <description>When being targeted during the shooting phase, vessels with this special rule count as being 5 cm further away from the attacking vessel than they are.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Covert Operatives" id="3f10-7d64-12e2-9220" hidden="false">
              <description>Once per battle at the beginning of your turn you may activate the covert operatives hidden amidst the enemy fl eet, giving all enemy vessels the Sabotaged condition until the beginning of your next turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="False Orders" id="e50c-3fcf-cb8e-039c" hidden="false">
              <description>When an enemy ship or squadron rolls doubles on a successful command check to go on a special order other than Brace For Impact!, instead of placing it on the declared special order, roll a D6 on the table to the right and place it on the corresponding special order. If this happens your opponent may use a commander&apos;s re-roll as if the ship had failed its command check. (Note: If you are using Special Order dice you can roll one instead of rolling on the chart.)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Blackshields" id="4d37-3165-3f4b-aa22" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade"/>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Upgrades" id="d350-396e-08cb-08c3" hidden="false">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Legion Veterans" id="3395-e490-05c1-70c9" hidden="true" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="f0b7-ab7b-dfc3-b8ee" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="a703-84df-1c7d-aae9" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="0"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="10"/>
          </costs>
          <infoGroups>
            <infoGroup name="New Info Group" id="4c5b-2ad5-fed3-c4bc" hidden="false">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Hold the Line" id="074c-b727-0e75-41da" hidden="false">
                  <description>A ship that has embarked Legion Veterans is never considered as having fewer than half its maximum number of damage points remaining for the purposes of determining its troop rating.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Chosen Warriors" id="5052-ef07-2a22-156c" hidden="false">
                  <description>Once per game when resolving Boarding Actions a ship that has embarked Legion Veterans may roll 2D6 (3D3 for Blood Angels vessels), discarding the lowest result (Blood Angels vessels choose two results instead).</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Boarding Specialists" id="32f7-e7df-ea0d-767b" hidden="false">
                  <description>Any Legion Capital ship that has embarked Legion Veterans may be equipped with Ursus Claws for +15 points.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </infoGroup>
          </infoGroups>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="4573636f72747323232344415441232323" childName="Escort" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" scope="parent" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
                <condition childId="f448-d70a-49e6-0c2f" childName="Heavy Escort" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" scope="parent" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Legion Terminators" id="5d90-72c1-bc6e-af0d" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="a567-0697-9a7a-e170" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
                <constraint id="dc52-17b0-ab6d-f3d6" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="0"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="25"/>
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Zone Mortalis Specialists" id="fa8d-c465-e00b-704d" hidden="false">
                  <description>On top of its normal bonuses for being a Legiones Astartes vessel the ship gains a +1 bonus to Teleport Hit-and-Run attacks and Boarding Actions, and imposes a -1 to enemy Hit-and-Run attacks.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Mass Teleport Attack" id="2d85-8a5d-d121-0556" hidden="false">
                  <description>When a vessel with Legion Terminators conducts a teleport attack, roll 3D6 (Blood Angels vessels roll 2D3 three times) and choose two results to apply.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Ursus Claws" id="f616-0daa-f3fe-075a" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="5229-19ec-f88b-d82e" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
                <constraint id="90b5-e233-5ba4-3538" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="0"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="15"/>
              </costs>
              <infoLinks>
                <infoLink name="Ursus Claws" id="d197-f2a7-8be2-ea4a" hidden="false" targetId="40d7-82be-7f9d-d942" type="rule"/>
              </infoLinks>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Add boarding torpedoes" id="55a0-74b4-7742-4f4b" hidden="true" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="c929-2e7e-4312-943b" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Boarding Torpedoes" id="8fe6-6109-4ea8-8c80" hidden="false" targetId="0ceb-108a-4241-00fb" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Add boarding torpedoes" id="f748-c77c-9e09-2871" hidden="true" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="d35f-2ce3-2d1b-c937" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="10"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Boarding Torpedoes" id="ef84-4dc7-6716-ae6b" hidden="false" targetId="0ceb-108a-4241-00fb" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Add boarding torpedoes" id="58c5-cb84-11ed-1e4c" hidden="true" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="afa5-e637-ce70-a4de" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Boarding Torpedoes" id="b7e9-8986-d205-4f1d" hidden="false" targetId="0ceb-108a-4241-00fb" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Engine refits" id="2bc3-9439-d3b1-22de" hidden="false">
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Secondary Reactors" id="3167-2b1c-d218-5783" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="b5fc-937c-9490-63b8" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.05"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="895a-5f48-1934-4ebf" childName="VIII Legion: Night Lords" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="7d26-72b3-f499-9f70" childName="XII Legion: World Eaters" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="6e9a-c8ea-9ea4-a1ef" childName="XVI Legion: Sons of Horus" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="ad76-0514-b1fe-e3ff" childName="XVII Legion: Word Bearers" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Secondary Reactors" id="e3fa-51d5-bef2-8cb8" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship’s additional power generators allow it to put on a tremendous burst of speed for short lengths of time. The ship adds an extra +2D6 cm to its speed when on All Ahead Full special orders</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Evasive Jets:" id="75c6-1640-d41f-18d5" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="2" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="7731-6498-c079-724c" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.05"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="9877-39a7-a969-7532" childName="XX Legion: Alpha Legion" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="1c53-dfe1-5fdb-606e" childName="XIII Legion: Ultramarines" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="133e-d08d-1476-0067" childName="XIX Legion: Ravenguard" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Evasive Jets:" id="214e-414f-f373-0b7e" hidden="false">
                  <description>The hull of the vessel is studded with powerful short-burn engines which allow it to drastically turn to avoid incoming fi re. At the start of the enemy shooting phase, the ship may take a leadership test. If the test is passed, the ship immediately turns 45° in the direction of your choice and cannot go on special orders during its next turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Maneuvering Thrusters" id="6080-bbcd-2c0d-91f4" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="3" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="df7f-c9be-2e8d-ec2b" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.1"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="c79a-7800-902e-fa2b" childName="III Legion: Emperor’s Children" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="6c6e-2e0d-d7f8-5208" childName="IX Legion: Blood Angels" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="8215-bb96-0b1c-a9ac" childName="V Legion: White Scars" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Maneuvering Thrusters" id="0cf7-378f-80fa-e0be" hidden="false">
                  <description>Additional thrusters along the length of the ship allow it to turn much more quickly. The ship reduces the distance it needs to move before turning by 5 cm.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Arrester Engines" id="1a27-4f9c-71ac-5fe0" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="4" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="cf0f-81ba-5a53-1bc2" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.025"/>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Arrester Engines" id="c651-6655-f907-d0d5" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship has a number of secondary engines mounted near its prow, which enable the vessel to reduce speed rapidly. The ship has +1 Ld while attempting to go on Burn Retros or Come to New Heading special orders</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Auxiliary Power Relays" id="bf59-b940-1e35-776f" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="5" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="cb0b-5ec1-d53c-ad5c" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.1"/>
                <modifier affects="profiles.Unit" field="5.370656564232324e+29" scope="root-entry" type="cumulative-add" value="5"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="9877-23f6-6b76-57be" childName="VI Legion: Space Wolves" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="6c6e-2e0d-d7f8-5208" childName="IX Legion: Blood Angels" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Auxiliary Power Relays" id="e35e-9c04-216c-7753" hidden="false">
                  <description>The rear of the ship is criss-crossed with additional cables and pipelines, feeding more power to the engines. The ship adds +5 cm to its speed</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Navigational Shields" id="4d05-a3df-dce8-dd27" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="6" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="1637-108f-5018-a934" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.05"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="133e-d08d-1476-0067" childName="XIX Legion: Ravenguard" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="9877-23f6-6b76-57be" childName="VI Legion: Space Wolves" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="7d26-72b3-f499-9f70" childName="XII Legion: World Eaters" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="2777-c660-0c69-7387" childName="XIV Legion: Death Guard" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Navigational Shields" id="b484-5593-e109-f8a6" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship is enveloped in low-frequency shields designed to shunt aside debris and other impediments as the ship moves. The ship does not suff er reductions to its speed for moving through blast markers (this includes gas, dust clouds, and similar eff ects)</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Ship refits" id="1704-c48c-20bf-8f75" hidden="false">
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Reinforced Hull" id="fd1c-596a-d207-8fac" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="4" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="7b5c-e3b3-62da-3dff" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.1"/>
                <modifier affects="profiles.Unit" field="4.869747323232344e+27" scope="root-entry" type="multiply" value="1.25"/>
                <modifier affects="profiles.Unit" field="5.370656564232324e+29" scope="root-entry" type="cumulative-add" value="-5"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="and">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="285d-f209-539b-f80a" childName="IV Legion: Iron Warriors" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="4573636f72747323232344415441232323" childName="Escort" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" scope="parent" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="f448-d70a-49e6-0c2f" childName="Heavy Escort" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" scope="parent" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Reinforced Hull" id="5f04-eac2-0a3b-8caf" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship’s hull is fi tted with additional armour and internal bracing, increasing the maximum damage points of the ship by 25% (rounding up), but reducing its Speed characteristic by 5 cm. Escorts cannot take this refit.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Superior Damage Control" id="c6eb-9af9-7239-9766" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="3" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="0431-0076-f314-89fe" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.025"/>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Superior Damage Control" id="705f-feed-5af3-9eef" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship benefits from an improved auto-repair system, or more highly adept engineers and technicians. The ship may roll an additional D6 when attempting to repair critical damage</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Overloaded Shield Capacitors" id="b2f0-53e3-6bbb-144b" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="6" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="6ecd-a351-f765-81e7" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.025"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="f504-3651-b642-7020" childName="I Legion: Dark Angels" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="e2ac-e571-0341-667b" childName="VII Legion: Imperial Fists" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="2777-c660-0c69-7387" childName="XIV Legion: Death Guard" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="59b5-999e-4d1b-fe68" childName="XV Legion: Thousand Sons" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Overloaded Shield Capacitors" id="c0f3-4ba6-fc9b-c74b" hidden="false">
                  <description>Specialised power relays and generators allow the ship’s engineers to temporarily divert extra power to the shields. For each hit against the ship’s shields, roll a D6. On a roll of a 6, the hit is ignored and no Blast Marker is placed. This refi t has no eff ect against hits that bypass shields.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Improved Sensor Array" id="3874-c99d-814f-3f3f" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="2763-a4a7-cc96-233e" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.025"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="9877-39a7-a969-7532" childName="XX Legion: Alpha Legion" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Improved Sensor Array" id="b2a5-796d-edde-f8f1" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship’s assayers and long range surveyors are particularly attuned to pick up energy emissions and signals from enemy Ships. The ship gains +2 Ld if any enemy ships are on special orders instead of only +1Ld.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Additional Shield Generator" id="0eb1-f125-a26d-ef0f" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="2" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="2d16-6009-cf0a-f9a3" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.1"/>
                <modifier affects="profiles.Unit" field="536869656c647323232344415441232323" scope="root-entry" type="cumulative-add" value="1"/>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Additional Shield Generator" id="86fc-e9b3-2d33-3ba7" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship has additional shield generators to defl ect incoming shots. The ship adds +1 to its Shields characteristic.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Improved Logic Engines" id="b668-4cab-c097-80b1" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="5" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="d1c6-fe7b-82aa-98c7" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.025"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="c79a-7800-902e-fa2b" childName="III Legion: Emperor’s Children" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="e2ac-e571-0341-667b" childName="VII Legion: Imperial Fists" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="6e9a-c8ea-9ea4-a1ef" childName="XVI Legion: Sons of Horus" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Improved Logic Engines" id="8f45-dfbe-692b-df5d" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship’s countless metriculators and mechanical cogitator enable the crew to perform with full eff ectiveness even in the midst of the fi ercest battle. The ship does not suff er -1 Ld to its command checks while in contact with blast markers.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Vox Scream Array" id="d740-0f11-e03a-e7a0" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="7" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="8c79-9b7f-e311-20db" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.05"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="895a-5f48-1934-4ebf" childName="VIII Legion: Night Lords" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Vox Scream Array" id="e313-7f0e-3eec-230f" hidden="false">
                  <description>At the beginning of your end phase this ship may designate one enemy capital ship or escort squadron within 30cm as the target of its Vox Scream infl icting the eff ects listed in the table below, however, no vessel may be targeted by more than one Vox Scream Array per turn. Because of their high energy needs ships cannot use their Vox Scream Array if they are crippled or if they are on All Ahead Full special orders. Escorts cannot take this refit.


Capital Ships and Defenses with 4 or more damage points
The target suffers a single Terror critical hit.
Escorts and Defenses with 3 or Fewer damage points
The target ship or squadron reduces its leadership by -1 for the next turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Weapons refits" id="372d-feaf-150a-ea4a" hidden="false">
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Motion-Tracking Targeters" id="14e0-4400-915a-7c53" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="6" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="7c90-f245-f2e2-e81b" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.05"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="8215-bb96-0b1c-a9ac" childName="V Legion: White Scars" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Motion-Tracking Targeters" id="f651-7384-9a7a-f78c" hidden="false">
                  <description>A complex analytical array linked to the ship’s navigational systems enables the gun crews to fi re with greater accuracy when the ship is performing special manoeuvres. If the ship is on All Ahead Full, Burn Retros, or Come to a New Heading special orders, its weapons’ eff ectiveness is reduced by only 25% (rounding up) rather than halved.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Targeting Matrix" id="24ca-e4a0-566d-0588" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="3" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="f5be-cd33-28e1-63dc" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.1"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="59b5-999e-4d1b-fe68" childName="XV Legion: Thousand Sons" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Targeting Matrix" id="52a3-a010-4381-a87f" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship’s weapon systems are linked together through a massive targeting network so that they can maximise their fi re. All gunnery weapons benefit from an extra left column-shift in addition to any other column-shifts that apply.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Auto-Loaders" id="f12a-2702-1e93-5a62" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="4" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="1b9b-90d3-e6c5-a855" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.025"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="1c53-dfe1-5fdb-606e" childName="XIII Legion: Ultramarines" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Auto-Loaders" id="5143-e505-5f49-b684" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship’s crew are aided in their task of readying torpedoes and attack craft by huge semi-automated machinery. The ship has +1 Ld while attempting command checks to go on Reload Ordnance special orders.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Extra Turrets" id="65c0-b06e-bd51-7603" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="9824-e87b-9a5c-a4db" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.025"/>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Extra Turrets" id="b90e-c620-3234-dbd9" hidden="false">
                  <description>The vessel is studded with numerous close defence weapons to shoot down enemy torpedoes and attack craft. This ship adds +1 to its Turrets value.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Turbo Weapons" id="81e8-c25a-9f9a-3b54" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="2" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="7f67-33a6-a78f-0a0b" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.05"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="f504-3651-b642-7020" childName="I Legion: Dark Angels" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="29c8-bcd9-5e13-4e18" childName="X Legion: Iron Hands" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="ad76-0514-b1fe-e3ff" childName="XVII Legion: Word Bearers" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                        <condition childId="c025-acff-a07e-b2f9" childName="XVIII Legion: Salamanders" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Turbo Weapons" id="f2ac-7831-aa20-6e82" hidden="false">
                  <description>The ship’s weapons have been given additional punch and accuracy at long range. The ship does not suff er a right column-shift when fi ring its weapons at targets more than 30 cm away.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Superior Fire Control" id="be01-fc46-55f1-ec6a" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="5" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="2972-9027-979a-ed6b" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.025"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="285d-f209-539b-f80a" childName="IV Legion: Iron Warriors" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Superior Fire Control" id="e9ad-c086-bd35-0ee6" hidden="false">
                  <description>A powerful fi re control system has been installed in the ship’s bridge, enabling the command crew to direct the ship’s fi ring with greater eff ect. The ship has +1 Ld while attempting command checks to go on Lock On special orders.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Archeotech Refit" id="cb15-4bd6-7429-4fa8" hidden="true" import="true" sortIndex="7" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="eef7-1b54-1a0e-ef34" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="points" scope="parent" type="multiply" value="1.1"/>
                <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="29c8-bcd9-5e13-4e18" childName="X Legion: Iron Hands" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Archeotech Refits" id="d316-c3f7-7756-637e" hidden="false">
                  <description>Some ships can be upgraded with Archeotech refi ts. When that is the case, roll on the following table.
1
Emergency Energy Reserves: When crippled, the ship only reduces turrets, shielding and weapons by 25% rather than 50%. The vessel still counts as crippled in every other respect.
2
Advanced Engines: The ship gains +5cm speed, as well as +1D6 when on All Ahead Full special orders.
3
Repulsor Shielding: Ignore all negative eff ects of having a blast marker or gas clouds in contact with the ship&apos;s base as it applies to leadership, movement and repairing critical damage. This eff ect goes away if the ship suff ers “Shields Collapsed” critical damage.
4
Fleet Defence Turrets: Up to two turrets on the ship are exchanged for fl eet defence turrets capable of protecting itself or any one other vessel within 15 cm each ordnance phase, adding +2 to the turret strength of the ship it is defending (this does not alter bomber attack rolls when used to defend another vessel). These otherwise work exactly as normal turrets do in all other respects.
5
Gyro-stabilized Targeting Matrix: Ship weapons are reduced to 75% instead of 50% when on All Ahead Full, Come To New Heading or Burn Retros special orders. Nova Cannons and Plasma Scourers still cannot fi re.
6
Augmented Weapon Relays: Weapon batteries shift left on the gunnery table before all other modifi ers are applied. Lance hits count double on rolls of a 6.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Commander Onboard" id="adec-b94f-ac0d-6426" hidden="true">
          <selectionEntries>
